<h2><span class="sec-num">1</span> Document Control</h2>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>Item</th><th>Value</th></tr>
<tr><td>Document</td><td>Functional Specification: Vendor Bank Details Validation &amp; Formatting Utility</td></tr>
<tr><td>Object (proposed)</td><td><code>ZCL_VENDOR_BANK_VALIDATOR</code> (global ABAP class). Exception class proposed: <code>ZCX_VENDOR_BANK_ERROR</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Object type</td><td>Reusable utility class (no UI, no transaction, no database writes)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Module</td><td>FI-AP / MM vendor master (bank data)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Target system</td><td>SAP ECC, SAP_BASIS 740, client 800. Design is compatible with SAP_BASIS 740 (no CDS-in-ABAP, AMDP, RAP or enums)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Version / Date</td><td>1.0 Draft, 23-Oct-2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>Status</td><td>Draft for business review</td></tr>
</table>
<div class="callout">No FS template is uploaded, so this document uses the standard C16 FS layout. The class name is a proposal. No custom class with this name exists yet: a search for <code>ZCL%BANK%</code> returned 14 unrelated objects, mostly OData DPC/MPC classes and training classes.</div>

<h2><span class="sec-num">2</span> Business Background &amp; Objective</h2>
<p>Several programs and interfaces create or check vendor bank details: vendor uploads, payment-run pre-checks, interface inbound validation and data-quality reports. Each one re-implements its own checks today, or skips them. The result is inconsistent bank data in the vendor master (table <code>LFBK</code>). That leads to rejected payment files and manual rework in Accounts Payable.</p>
<p>The objective is <strong>one central, reusable class</strong> that any custom program can call to:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Validate</strong> a vendor's bank country, bank key and bank account number against the country rules configured in SAP (OY17 / table <code>T005</code>) and against the bank master (FI01 / table <code>BNKA</code>).</li>
<li><strong>Format</strong> these values consistently: normalised for storage, masked for display, and as IBAN where the country supports it.</li>
<li>Return <strong>clear, translatable messages</strong> that the caller can show, log or reject on.</li>
</ol>

