<h3>3.3 Country check rules configured (T005, OY17)</h3>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>Country</th><th>Bank Key type (BNKEY)</th><th>Bank key length / rule</th><th>Bank number length / rule</th><th>Account length / rule</th><th>Bank data flag (XPRBK)</th></tr>
<tr><td>DE</td><td>1 – Bank number</td><td>00 / –</td><td>08 / 4</td><td>14 / 2</td><td>X</td></tr>
<tr><td>AT</td><td>1 – Bank number</td><td>00 / –</td><td>05 / 4</td><td>11 / 2</td><td>X</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR</td><td>1 – Bank number</td><td>00 / –</td><td>10 / 4</td><td>11 / 3</td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>IT</td><td>1 – Bank number</td><td>00 / –</td><td>10 / 4</td><td>12 / 5</td><td>X</td></tr>
<tr><td>ES</td><td>1 – Bank number</td><td>00 / –</td><td>08 / 4</td><td>10 / 4</td><td>X</td></tr>
<tr><td>GB</td><td>1 – Bank number</td><td>00 / –</td><td>06 / 1</td><td>08 / 1</td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>US</td><td>1 – Bank number</td><td>00 / –</td><td>09 / 4</td><td>13 / 0</td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>CA</td><td>1 – Bank number</td><td>10 / 5</td><td>10 / 5</td><td>10 / 5</td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>CH</td><td>1 – Bank number</td><td>07 / 2</td><td>07 / 2</td><td>18 / 5</td><td>X</td></tr>
<tr><td>BE</td><td>4 – Assign externally</td><td>03 / 3</td><td>00 / –</td><td>14 / 3</td><td>X</td></tr>
<tr><td>NL</td><td>4 – Assign externally</td><td>05 / 1</td><td>00 / –</td><td>10 / 4</td><td>X</td></tr>
<tr><td>IN</td><td>4 – Assign externally</td><td>11 / 1</td><td>15 / 5</td><td>00 / –</td><td></td></tr>
</table>
<h3>3.4 Check-rule values (domain PR005)</h3>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>Rule</th><th>Meaning (DDIC text)</th><th>Utility behaviour</th></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td>Maximum value length, without gaps</td><td>len ≤ L; no blanks</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>Maximum value length, numerical, without gaps</td><td>len ≤ L; digits only</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td>Length to be kept to exactly, without gaps</td><td>len = L; no blanks</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td>Length to be kept to exactly, numerical, without gaps</td><td>len = L; digits only</td></tr>
<tr><td>5</td><td>Maximum value length</td><td>len ≤ L (blanks allowed)</td></tr>
<tr><td>6</td><td>Maximum value length, numerical</td><td>len ≤ L; digits and blanks only</td></tr>
<tr><td>7</td><td>Length to be kept to exactly</td><td>len = L</td></tr>
<tr><td>8</td><td>Length to be kept to exactly, numerical</td><td>len = L; digits and blanks only</td></tr>
<tr><td>9</td><td>Check against country-specific edit format</td><td>Delegate to the SAP standard check (see FR-07)</td></tr>
<tr><td>0 / blank</td><td>No check (0 is "Deactivate check" for USA)</td><td>Skip the rule check (length L is still informative only)</td></tr>
</table>
<div class="callout warning"><strong>Findings that justify this utility:</strong> (1) There are LFBK records with no vendor number, one of them fully blank. (2) The IN record uses bank key <code>B 111</code>, which breaks the IN rule 1 ("without gaps") and has no BNKA entry. (3) The same bank key (e.g. <code>20050000</code>, <code>1234</code>) exists under several countries (DE/AR, DK/IN/UG). The bank key is only unique <strong>together with the bank country</strong>, so every lookup must use both.</div>

<h2><span class="sec-num">4</span> Scope</h2>
<h3>4.1 In scope</h3>
<ul>
<li>Validation of bank country (<code>BANKS</code>), bank key (<code>BANKL</code>), bank account (<code>BANKN</code>) and, optionally, bank control key (<code>BKONT</code>).</li>
<li>Normalisation (storage format), display formatting (masked and full) and IBAN derivation.</li>
<li>A single "validate all" call that returns every finding at once, so the caller does not stop at the first error.</li>
<li>Read-only access to the configuration and master data in <code>T005</code>, <code>BNKA</code>, <code>TIBAN</code> and <code>LFBK</code>.</li>
</ul>
<h3>4.2 Out of scope</h3>
<ul>
<li>Creating or changing vendor master or bank master data. The class never writes to the database.</li>
<li>Payment-medium formats (DMEE), house-bank data and customer bank data. The design could be extended to <code>KNBK</code> later.</li>
<li>Any UI, selection screen or report. Callers own the presentation.</li>
<li>External bank-directory or IBAN web-service lookups.</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="sec-num">5</span> Data Objects Used (DDIC-verified)</h2>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>Table</th><th>Field</th><th>Data element</th><th>Label (DD04T)</th><th>Type / length</th><th>Use</th></tr>
<tr><td>LFBK</td><td>LIFNR</td><td>LIFNR</td><td>Vendor</td><td>CHAR 10</td><td>Vendor-level check (optional input)</td></tr>
<tr><td>LFBK</td><td>BANKS</td><td>BANKS</td><td>Bank Country</td><td>CHAR 3</td><td>Input</td></tr>
<tr><td>LFBK</td><td>BANKL</td><td>BANKK</td><td>Bank Key</td><td>CHAR 15</td><td>Input</td></tr>
<tr><td>LFBK</td><td>BANKN</td><td>BANKN</td><td>Bank Account</td><td>CHAR 18</td><td>Input</td></tr>
<tr><td>LFBK</td><td>BKONT</td><td>BKONT</td><td>Bank control key</td><td>CHAR 2</td><td>Optional input (IBAN / FR, ES, IT)</td></tr>
<tr><td>LFBK</td><td>BKREF</td><td>BKREF</td><td>Reference details</td><td>CHAR 20</td><td>Overflow for accounts over 18 characters (information only)</td></tr>
<tr><td>LFBK</td><td>KOINH</td><td>KOINH_FI</td><td>Account holder</td><td>CHAR 60</td><td>Optional completeness warning</td></tr>
<tr><td>T005</td><td>BNKEY</td><td>BNKEY</td><td>Bank Key</td><td>CHAR 1</td><td>How the bank key is assigned (1 = bank number, 4 = external, …)</td></tr>
<tr><td>T005</td><td>LNBKS / PRBKS</td><td>LNBKS_005 / PRBKS_005</td><td>Length of Bank Key / Check rule for bank key</td><td>NUMC 2 / CHAR 1</td><td>Bank key rule</td></tr>
<tr><td>T005</td><td>LNBLZ / PRBLZ</td><td>LNBLZ_005 / PRBLZ_005</td><td>Bank number length / Check rule for bank number</td><td>NUMC 2 / CHAR 1</td><td>Bank number rule (applies to the key when BNKEY = 1)</td></tr>
<tr><td>T005</td><td>LNBKN / PRBKN</td><td>LNBKN_005 / PRBKN_005</td><td>Bank account number length / Check rule for bank acct no.</td><td>NUMC 2 / CHAR 1</td><td>Account rule</td></tr>
<tr><td>T005</td><td>XPRBK</td><td>XPRBK_005</td><td>Bank data</td><td>CHAR 1</td><td>Country needs additional country-specific bank checks</td></tr>
<tr><td>BNKA</td><td>BANKS, BANKL</td><td>BANKS, BANKK</td><td>Bank Country, Bank Key</td><td>CHAR 3, 15</td><td>Bank master existence (key = country + key)</td></tr>
<tr><td>BNKA</td><td>BANKA / SWIFT / BNKLZ</td><td>BANKA / SWIFT / BANKL</td><td>Bank name / SWIFT/BIC / Bank number</td><td>CHAR 60 / 11 / 15</td><td>Enrichment and IBAN input</td></tr>
<tr><td>BNKA</td><td>LOEVM</td><td>LOEVM</td><td>Deletion flag</td><td>CHAR 1</td><td>Reject banks flagged for deletion</td></tr>
<tr><td>TIBAN</td><td>IBAN, BANKS, BANKL, BANKN, BKONT</td><td>IBAN, …</td><td>IBAN</td><td>CHAR 34</td><td>Look up an IBAN already stored for the account</td></tr>
</table>

<h2><span class="sec-num">6</span> Functional Requirements</h2>
<h3>6.1 Validation requirements</h3>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>ID</th><th>Requirement</th><th>Rule / logic</th><th>Severity on failure</th></tr>
<tr><td>FR-01</td><td>Bank country is mandatory and must exist</td><td>BANKS not initial and found in T005 (key LAND1). Input is converted to upper case first.</td><td>Error</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-02</td><td>Bank key is mandatory</td><td>BANKL not initial after trimming.</td><td>Error</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-03</td><td>Bank key format follows the country rule</td><td>If T005-BNKEY = 1 (bank key = bank number): apply LNBLZ/PRBLZ to the key. Otherwise apply LNBKS/PRBKS. Use the check-rule logic in §3.4.</td><td>Error</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-04</td><td>Bank key exists in the bank master</td><td>Read BNKA with <strong>BANKS + BANKL</strong> (never BANKL alone). Not found → error. Found with LOEVM = 'X' → error "bank flagged for deletion".</td><td>Error</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-05</td><td>Bank account is mandatory where the country uses accounts</td><td>If T005-LNBKN = 00 and PRBKN is blank (e.g. IN), the account is not rule-checked, but an empty account still gives a warning.</td><td>Error (Warning for LNBKN = 00)</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-06</td><td>Bank account format follows the country rule</td><td>Apply LNBKN/PRBKN using the §3.4 logic. Rule 0 or blank → no check.</td><td>Error</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-07</td><td>Country-specific standard checks</td><td>Call the SAP standard function <code>BANK_NUMBER_CHECK</code> (verified signature: BANK_ACCOUNT, BANK_COUNTRY, BANK_NUMBER; exceptions DATA_MISSING, NOT_VALID) so SAP's own country algorithms also run. Required when rule = 9 or T005-XPRBK = 'X'; recommended always. Its exceptions are mapped to the class's own messages.</td><td>Error</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-08</td><td>Control key plausibility</td><td>If BKONT is supplied: max 2 characters, no gaps. For countries that use control keys (e.g. FR, sample vendor 0000000010 with BKONT 11), a missing BKONT gives a warning.</td><td>Warning</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-09</td><td>Vendor-level duplicate check (optional)</td><td>When a vendor (LIFNR) is supplied, report if the same BANKS + BANKL + BANKN already exists in LFBK for a <em>different</em> vendor. This can point to fraud or a duplicate vendor.</td><td>Warning</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-10</td><td>Collect all findings</td><td><code>VALIDATE_ALL</code> runs every check and returns the complete list (no early exit), with an overall valid / invalid flag.</td><td>–</td></tr>
</table>
<h3>6.2 Formatting requirements</h3>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>ID</th><th>Requirement</th><th>Example (from live data)</th></tr>
<tr><td>FR-11</td><td><strong>Normalise</strong> for storage: convert country to upper case, trim leading and trailing blanks, remove common separators (space, "-", "/", ".") from the key and account <em>only when the country rule is "without gaps" or numerical</em>. No zero-padding unless the rule is "exact length, numerical" and the business enables padding (open point OP-02).</td><td>"de" → "DE"; "5656-5656" → "56565656"</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-12</td><td><strong>Mask</strong> the account for display: show only the last 4 characters and mask the rest with "*". The mask length equals the original length.</td><td>"88888888" → "****8888"</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-13</td><td><strong>Display string</strong>: "&lt;country&gt; / &lt;bank key&gt; / &lt;account (masked by default)&gt; – &lt;bank name&gt;"</td><td>"DE / 56565656 / ****8888 – City-Bank Hamburg"</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-14</td><td><strong>IBAN</strong>: first read TIBAN for an IBAN already stored for BANKS/BANKL/BANKN/BKONT. Otherwise derive it with the SAP standard function <code>CONVERT_BANK_ACCOUNT_2_IBAN</code> (verified: I_BANK_ACCOUNT, I_BANK_CONTROL_KEY, I_BANK_COUNTRY, I_BANK_NUMBER = BNKA-BNKLZ, I_BANK_KEY; E_IBAN; exception NO_CONVERSION). If no conversion is possible, return an empty IBAN plus an information message, not an error.</td><td>DE / 56565656 / 88888888 → IBAN derived by the SAP standard algorithm</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-15</td><td><strong>Bank details enrichment</strong>: return bank name, SWIFT/BIC and bank number from BNKA.</td><td>DK / 1234 → "Danske Bank A/S", DABADKKK</td></tr>
<tr><td>FR-16</td><td>Formatting methods never change their input. They return new values.</td><td>–</td></tr>
</table>

<h2><span class="sec-num">7</span> Proposed Public Interface (functional view)</h2>
<p>The developer finalises the exact signatures in the Technical Specification. All types refer to DDIC data elements (BANKS, BANKK, BANKN, BKONT, LIFNR, IBAN, BANKA, SWIFT, BAPIRET2).</p>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>Method</th><th>Inputs</th><th>Outputs</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>VALIDATE_ALL</code></td><td>Bank country, bank key, bank account, control key (opt.), vendor (opt.)</td><td>Valid flag + message table (BAPIRET2)</td><td>Runs FR-01 to FR-10 in one call</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>VALIDATE_BANK_COUNTRY</code></td><td>Bank country</td><td>Valid flag + messages</td><td>FR-01</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>VALIDATE_BANK_KEY</code></td><td>Bank country, bank key</td><td>Valid flag + messages</td><td>FR-02 to FR-04</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>VALIDATE_ACCOUNT_NUMBER</code></td><td>Bank country, bank key, account, control key (opt.)</td><td>Valid flag + messages</td><td>FR-05 to FR-08</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>NORMALIZE</code></td><td>Bank country, bank key, account</td><td>Normalised values</td><td>FR-11</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>MASK_ACCOUNT</code></td><td>Account</td><td>Masked account</td><td>FR-12</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>FORMAT_FOR_DISPLAY</code></td><td>Bank country, bank key, account, show-full flag (default off)</td><td>Display string</td><td>FR-13</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>GET_IBAN</code></td><td>Bank country, bank key, account, control key</td><td>IBAN + messages</td><td>FR-14</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>GET_BANK_DETAILS</code></td><td>Bank country, bank key</td><td>Bank name, SWIFT/BIC, bank number, found flag</td><td>FR-15</td></tr>
</table>
<div class="callout tip"><strong>Testability (required):</strong> All database reads (T005, BNKA, TIBAN, LFBK) sit behind a local data-access interface that is injected through the constructor. ABAP Unit tests can then supply fake configuration and edge-case rows. On SAP_BASIS 740 the SQL test-double framework is not available, so a classic dependency-injection fake is required. Country rules are buffered per call sequence, with one T005 read per country per instance.</div>

