nsform="translate(304.8671875, 2053.671875)"><rect class="basic label-container" style="" x="-130" y="-51" width="260" height="102"></rect><g class="label" style="" transform="translate(-100, -36)"><rect></rect><foreignObject width="200" height="72"><div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="display: table; white-space: break-spaces; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center; width: 200px;"><span class="nodeLabel "><p>Return valid flag = no E messages, plus full message table</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g><g class="node default  " id="flowchart-D-9" transform="translate(440.60546875, 612.859375)"><rect class="basic label-container" style="" x="-130" y="-63" width="260" height="126"></rect><g class="label" style="" transform="translate(-100, -48)"><rect></rect><foreignObject width="200" height="96"><div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="display: table; white-space: break-spaces; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center; width: 200px;"><span class="nodeLabel "><p>Read country rules: BNKEY, LNBKS/PRBKS, LNBLZ/PRBLZ, LNBKN/PRBKN, XPRBK</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g><g class="node default  " id="flowchart-F-11" transform="translate(440.60546875, 799.6953125)"><polygon points="73.8359375,0 147.671875,-73.8359375 73.8359375,-147.671875 0,-73.8359375" class="label-container" transform="translate(-73.3359375, 73.8359375)"></polygon><g class="label" style="" transform="translate(-46.8359375, -12)"><rect></rect><foreignObject width="93.671875" height="24"><div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="display: table-cell; white-space: nowrap; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center;"><span class="nodeLabel "><p>BANKL filled?</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g><g class="node default  " id="flowchart-E2-13" transform="translate(293.828125, 1138.53125)"><rect class="basic label-container" style="" x="-113.5546875" y="-27" width="227.109375" height="54"></rect><g class="label" style="" transform="translate(-83.5546875, -12)"><rect></rect><foreignObject width="167.109375" height="24"><div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="display: table-cell; white-space: nowrap; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center;"><span class="nodeLabel "><p>Error: bank key missing</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g><g class="node default  " id="flowchart-G-15" transform="translate(587.3828125, 998.53125)"><rect class="basic label-container" style="" x="-130" y="-51" width="260" height="102"></rect><g class="label" style="" transform="translate(-100, -36)"><rect></rect><foreignObject width="200" height="72"><div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="display: table; white-space: break-spaces; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center; width: 200px;"><span class="nodeLabel "><p>Apply key rule: BNKEY=1 uses LNBLZ/PRBLZ, else LNBKS/PRBKS</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g><g class="node default  " id="flowchart-H-17" transform="translate(587.3828125, 1138.53125)"><rect class="basic label-container" style="" x="-130" y="-39" width="260" height="78"></rect><g class="label" style="" transform="translate(-100, -24)"><rect></rect><foreignObject width="200" height="48"><div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="display: table; white-space: break-spaces; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center; width: 200px;"><span class="nodeLabel "><p>Read BNKA by BANKS + BANKL; check LOEVM</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g><g class="node default  " id="flowchart-I-19" transform="translate(440.60546875, 1290.53125)"><rect class="basic label-container" style="" x="-130" y="-39" width="260" height="78"></rect><g class="label" style="" transform="translate(-100, -24)"><rect></rect><foreignObject width="200" height="48"><div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="display: table; white-space: break-spaces; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center; width: 200px;"><span class="nodeLabel "><p>Apply account rule LNBKN/PRBKN</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g><g class="node default  " id="flowchart-J-23" transform="translate(440.60546875, 1418.53125)"><rect class="basic label-container" style="" x="-130" y="-39" width="260" height="78"></rect><g class="label" style="" transform="translate(-100, -24)"><rect></rect><foreignObject width="200" height="48"><div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="display: table; white-space: break-spaces; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center; width: 200px;"><span class="nodeLabel "><p>Call BANK_NUMBER_CHECK if XPRBK=X or rule 9</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g><g class="node default  " id="flowchart-K-25" transform="translate(440.60546875, 1546.53125)"><rect class="basic label-container" style="" x="-130" y="-39" width="260" height="78"></rect><g class="label" style="" transform="translate(-100, -24)"><rect></rect><foreignObject width="200" height="48"><div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="display: table; white-space: break-spaces; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center; width: 200px;"><span class="nodeLabel "><p>Control key plausibility FR-08</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g><g class="node default  " id="flowchart-L-27" transform="translate(440.60546875, 1718.1015625)"><polygon points="82.5703125,0 165.140625,-82.5703125 82.5703125,-165.140625 0,-82.5703125" class="label-container" transform="translate(-82.0703125, 82.5703125)"></polygon><g class="label" style="" transform="translate(-55.5703125, -12)"><rect></rect><foreignObject width="111.140625" height="24"><div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="display: table-cell; white-space: nowrap; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center;"><span class="nodeLabel "><p>LIFNR supplied?</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g><g class="node default  " id="flowchart-M-29" transform="translate(527.8046875, 1913.671875)"><rect class="basic label-container" style="" x="-130" y="-39" width="260" height="78"></rect><g class="label" style="" transform="translate(-100, -24)"><rect></rect><foreignObject width="200" height="48"><div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="display: table; white-space: break-spaces; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center; width: 200px;"><span class="nodeLabel "><p>Duplicate account at other vendor? FR-09</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g></g></g></g></svg></figure>
<ol>
<li>Normalise all inputs (FR-11). Validation always runs on the normalised values.</li>
<li>Country check. If it fails, stop the country-dependent checks because there are no rules to apply, and return.</li>
<li>Bank key checks (format rule, then BNKA existence and deletion flag).</li>
<li>Account checks (format rule, then the standard country check).</li>
<li>Optional checks (control key, duplicate at another vendor).</li>
<li>Overall result is valid if no message has type E or A. Warnings (W) and information (I) do not make the result invalid.</li>
</ol>

<h2><span class="sec-num">9</span> Messages</h2>
<p>Proposed message class <code>ZVBANK</code>. All texts are T100 messages, so they are translatable. Numbers are proposals.</p>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>No.</th><th>Type</th><th>Text</th><th>Trigger</th></tr>
<tr><td>001</td><td>E</td><td>Bank country &amp;1 is missing or does not exist</td><td>FR-01</td></tr>
<tr><td>002</td><td>E</td><td>Bank key is missing</td><td>FR-02</td></tr>
<tr><td>003</td><td>E</td><td>Bank key &amp;1 violates rule &amp;2 (length &amp;3) for country &amp;4</td><td>FR-03</td></tr>
<tr><td>004</td><td>E</td><td>Bank key &amp;1 does not exist in the bank master for country &amp;2</td><td>FR-04</td></tr>
<tr><td>005</td><td>E</td><td>Bank &amp;1 / &amp;2 is flagged for deletion</td><td>FR-04</td></tr>
<tr><td>006</td><td>E</td><td>Bank account is missing</td><td>FR-05</td></tr>
<tr><td>007</td><td>E</td><td>Bank account violates rule &amp;1 (length &amp;2) for country &amp;3</td><td>FR-06</td></tr>
<tr><td>008</td><td>E</td><td>Bank account is not valid for country &amp;1 (SAP country check)</td><td>FR-07 (NOT_VALID)</td></tr>
<tr><td>009</td><td>W</td><td>Bank control key missing or implausible for country &amp;1</td><td>FR-08</td></tr>
<tr><td>010</td><td>W</td><td>Account already used by vendor &amp;1</td><td>FR-09</td></tr>
<tr><td>011</td><td>I</td><td>No IBAN can be derived for this account</td><td>FR-14</td></tr>
<tr><td>012</td><td>W</td><td>Bank account not checked: country &amp;1 has no account rule</td><td>FR-05</td></tr>
</table>

<h2><span class="sec-num">10</span> Error Handling</h2>
<ul>
<li>Business validation failures are <strong>returned as messages</strong> and never raised as exceptions. The caller decides whether to block, warn or log.</li>
<li>Technical failures, such as an unexpected exception from a standard function, raise <code>ZCX_VENDOR_BANK_ERROR</code> (inherits from CX_STATIC_CHECK, T100-based). The original exception is attached as PREVIOUS.</li>
<li>The class never shows a popup and never uses MESSAGE ... TYPE 'E'. It is safe for batch jobs, RFC and background runs.</li>
<li>Empty input never causes a short dump. Every read handles "not found" explicitly.</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="sec-num">11</span> Authorisation &amp; Data Protection</h2>
<ul>
<li>The class reads configuration and master data and does not perform its own authority check. The <strong>calling program</strong> is responsible for vendor-level authorisation (e.g. F_LFA1_BEK / F_LFA1_BUK) before it passes vendor data.</li>
<li>Bank account numbers are sensitive personal and financial data. Display formatting is <strong>masked by default</strong> (FR-12/13). Full display needs the caller to pass the show-full flag explicitly.</li>
<li>Account numbers are never written to application logs in clear text. Callers that log messages should use the masked form.</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="sec-num">12</span> Non-Functional Requirements</h2>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>Area</th><th>Requirement</th></tr>
<tr><td>Performance</td><td>One validation runs in under 50 ms. Country rules and bank master entries are buffered inside the instance. Mass callers can reuse one instance for thousands of records, e.g. all 1,231 LFBK rows.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Compatibility</td><td>SAP_BASIS 740: inline declarations and constructor expressions allowed; no REDUCE, enums, AMDP, CDS-in-ABAP or RAP.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Reusability</td><td>Independent of vendor vs customer. Bank checks take only country, key and account, so they can be reused later for KNBK.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Quality</td><td>ATC clean (no priority 1/2 findings). ABAP Unit coverage of every FR, using the injected data-access fake.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Translation</td><td>All user-facing texts are T100 messages; no hard-coded literals.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2><span class="sec-num">13</span> Test Scenarios (grounded in live data)</h2>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>#</th><th>Category</th><th>Input (country / key / account / control)</th><th>Expected result</th></tr>
<tr><td>T01</td><td>Positive</td><td>DE / 56565656 / 88888888 (vendor 0000000001)</td><td>Valid. Key: 8 digits = DE rule 4 exact 8. Account: 8 digits, within DE rule 2 max 14. Bank "City-Bank Hamburg"</td></tr>
<tr><td>T02</td><td>Positive</td><td>DE / 30080000 / 1234321 (vendor 0000000100)</td><td>Valid (7-digit account allowed under the "maximum" rule)</td></tr>
<tr><td>T03</td><td>Positive</td><td>FR / 3000200650 / 11111111111 / 11 (vendor 0000000010)</td><td>Valid on length rules (key exact 10 numeric; account exact 11). Bank "Credit Lyonnais"</td></tr>
<tr><td>T04</td><td>Negative</td><td>IN / "B 111" / 8888777788787 (LFBK record with no vendor)</td><td>Error 003 (IN rule 1 "without gaps") and Error 004 (not in BNKA for IN)</td></tr>
<tr><td>T05</td><td>Negative</td><td>blank / blank / blank (empty LFBK record)</td><td>Error 001; country-dependent checks skipped; no dump</td></tr>
<tr><td>T06</td><td>Negative</td><td>DE / 5656565 (7 digits) / 88888888</td><td>Error 003: DE requires exactly 8 numeric digits</td></tr>
<tr><td>T07</td><td>Negative</td><td>DE / 56565656 / 8888A888</td><td>Error 007: DE account rule 2 is numerical</td></tr>
<tr><td>T08</td><td>Boundary</td><td>DE / 56565656 / 14-digit account vs 15-digit account</td><td>14 digits valid; 15 digits → Error 007</td></tr>
<tr><td>T09</td><td>Boundary</td><td>AR / 20050000 vs DE / 20050000</td><td>Both found, but with different banks (Citibank vs Deutsche Bank Hamburg). Proves the lookup uses country + key</td></tr>
<tr><td>T10</td><td>Edge</td><td>US / &lt;valid key&gt; / any account</td><td>US account rule "0" → no format check on the account</td></tr>
<tr><td>T11</td><td>Edge</td><td>IN / valid key / blank account</td><td>Warning 012 only (IN has no account rule); result still valid</td></tr>
<tr><td>T12</td><td>Formatting</td><td>MASK_ACCOUNT( "88888888" )</td><td>"****8888"</td></tr>
<tr><td>T13</td><td>Formatting</td><td>NORMALIZE( "de" / " 5656-5656 " / "8888 8888" )</td><td>"DE" / "56565656" / "88888888"</td></tr>
<tr><td>T14</td><td>Formatting</td><td>GET_BANK_DETAILS( DK / 1234 )</td><td>"Danske Bank A/S", SWIFT DABADKKK</td></tr>
<tr><td>T15</td><td>Duplicate</td><td>Vendor 0000001003 with DE / 23984899 / 12345678</td><td>Warning 010: account already used by vendor 0000001002</td></tr>
<tr><td>T16</td><td>Regression</td><td>VALIDATE_ALL on T04 input</td><td>Returns <em>both</em> errors (003 and 004), with no early exit</td></tr>
</table>

<h2><span class="sec-num">14</span> Assumptions &amp; Open Points</h2>
<table class="data">
<tr><th>ID</th><th>Topic</th><th>Question / Assumption</th><th>Owner</th></tr>
<tr><td>OP-01</td><td>Naming</td><td>Confirm the class name <code>ZCL_VENDOR_BANK_VALIDATOR</code>, the exception class <code>ZCX_VENDOR_BANK_ERROR</code>, message class <code>ZVBANK</code> and the target package.</td><td>Dev lead</td></tr>
<tr><td>OP-02</td><td>Zero-padding</td><td>Should normalisation left-pad numeric "exact length" keys or accounts (e.g. DE bank key, FR account) or reject them as too short? Default assumption: reject, no padding.</td><td>AP business</td></tr>
<tr><td>OP-03</td><td>XPRBK meaning</td><td>Assumed meaning: XPRBK = 'X' requires the additional SAP country check (FR-07). Confirm against OY17 for the countries in use.</td><td>FI config</td></tr>
<tr><td>OP-04</td><td>Duplicates</td><td>Should a duplicate account at another vendor (FR-09) be a warning or a hard error?</td><td>AP / Compliance</td></tr>
<tr><td>OP-05</td><td>Data clean-up</td><td>The LFBK records with blank vendor numbers (§3.2) are a data-quality issue outside this object. Raise a separate clean-up item.</td><td>Master data team</td></tr>
<tr><td>OP-06</td><td>DK rules</td><td>The DK check rules were not part of the T005 extract above. Include them in the TS once confirmed.</td><td>FI config</td></tr>
</table>

